{
  "abstract": "For n at least three, a finite simple undirected graph on 3n vertices has real adjacency rank at most five if the sum of squared differences between its decreasing ordered adjacency eigenvalues and (2n, 0, ..., 0, -n, -n) is strictly less than 2/3. This answers Jovanović, Sedlar and Škrekovski's Problem 21 without a connectedness requirement. The proof reduces to nonsingular principal submatrices of orders six or seven and uses exact Lean-checked finite certificates.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jaime Nistal"
    }
  ],
